# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── build & tooling
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── secrets
# Never commit these, and never print their values into logs or transcripts.
*.env
*.env.*
!*.env.example
/key.env.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATA THAT DOES NOT GO TO A REMOTE
#
# Everything below is either confidential, licensed to this site only, or
# third-party material we have no right to redistribute. This is independent
# of the repository's own MIT license (see LICENSE) — these are someone
# else's material, or in-house data, and stay out regardless. The code in
# this repository is designed to run without it: the tests that need it skip
# with a message (see test/fixtures.mjs and test/corpus/loader.mjs), and
# scripts/spec-drift.mjs reports an empty registry.
#
# Flip any single line here only with a deliberate decision to redistribute
# that specific material.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Every EDID working file, wherever it ends up. This is the actual data format
# (see README) — belt-and-suspenders on top of the path-based rules below, so
# a `.ddc` dropped anywhere by accident (repo root during manual testing, a
# stray export, a future test fixture) can never be committed by mistake.
*.ddc

# Ground-truth corpus — 1,397 production monitor EDIDs, internal EDID List
# spec spreadsheets (two of them DRM-locked) and competitor captures.
/corpus/

# Everything under reference/ is evidence, not source:
#   specs/       43 VESA / CTA / HDMI standard PDFs, licensed per-seat, plus
#                the LLM extractions derived from them
#   decompiled/  Quantum Data ATP Manager plugin JARs run through CFR
#   samples/     30 DATAOBJ XML fixtures shipped with the ATP Manager instrument
#   rules/       in-house EDID review checklist
#   port/        the reference Python decoder this project ported from
# The pattern is `/reference/*`, not `/reference/`, so that one subfolder can
# be re-included later: git cannot un-ignore anything inside an excluded
# *directory*. To make `npm test` runnable on a private clone, append
#     !/reference/samples/
/reference/*

# Third-party binaries (cfr.jar — the Java decompiler, MIT).
/tools/

# Working EDID files. projects/ is the server's default working directory,
# so the folder itself is tracked while its contents are not.
/projects/*
!/projects/.gitkeep
